From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: video: fix negative array index when ISP node lacks id

viv_find_compatible_nodes() left `id` at its -1 sentinel value whenever
an ISP-compatible devicetree node was available but had no explicit
"id" property, and viv_video_probe()'s bounds check only rejected
video_id >= VIDEO_NODE_NUM, never negative values. That -1 flowed
straight into file_list_lock[-1] and vdev->id, so any userspace open()
of the resulting /dev/videoN node (e.g. udev's v4l_id) read one
spinlock_t before the array into whatever kernel memory happened to
be there, corrupting it and crashing (invalid access in
video_open()'s spin_lock_irqsave, fault address varying per boot with
KASLR). The crash then cascades into RCU stalls and a total system
hang within a couple of minutes.

isp_hw_probe() in isp_driver_of.c already defaults a missing "id" to 0
for exactly this reason (`isp device id not found, use the default.`);
do the same here, and reject negative ids defensively alongside the
existing overflow check.

Hit on imx8mp-cargt-00377-00365 with the -glt1011280800is1 and -hdmi
board dts variants, both of which pull in
imx8mp-cargt-00377-00365-os08a20.dtsi (`&isp_0 { status = "okay"; };`,
no id property set).

Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 video/video.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/video/video.c b/video/video.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/video/video.c
+++ b/video/video.c
@@ -2079,6 +2079,7 @@ static inline int viv_find_compatible_nodes(struct dev_node *nodes, int size)
 			rc = fwnode_property_read_u32(
 					of_fwnode_handle(node), "id", &id);
 			if (rc) {
+				id = 0;
 				if (of_device_is_available(node))
 					avail = node;
 			} else if (of_device_is_available(node))
@@ -2116,7 +2117,7 @@ static int viv_video_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	for (i = 0; i < nodecount; i++) {
 		if (nodes[i].node) {
 			video_id = nodes[i].id ;
-			if(video_id >= VIDEO_NODE_NUM) {
+			if (video_id < 0 || video_id >= VIDEO_NODE_NUM) {
 				pr_err("%s: id %d is too large (id > %d) \n",
 						__func__, video_id, VIDEO_NODE_NUM);
 				rc = -EINVAL;
